  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Disabling 'Eyes & Eyelids' in the Animator Tracking Control component can leave an avatar stuck partway through a blink (due to the simple movement-pausing method of the component), which causes jank and clipping issues when mixed with expressions that affect the eyes.\n\nNow, since the automated eye tracking/blinking is calculated entirely locally from my understanding, this would mean each remote client is essentially its own dice roll for whether or not the eyelids are broken for anyone anywhere in an instance after entering a synced expression that involves disabling eye movement/blinking (provided your avatar is visible to them). The more users in a lobby, the higher the chance your avatar is currently broken for *someone*.\n\nAdditionally, there should be a minimum delay before the first blink after re-enabling 'Eye & Eyelids' to allow for an expression to be exited before blend shape stacking can occur.",
